      <div type="clause" n="64">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 64</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="64" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="352" ed="#liebermann"/>Husbryce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.3-3"/> ⁊ bærnet ⁊ open þyfð ⁊ æbǽre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.4-3"/> morð ⁊ hlafordswyce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.5-3"/> æfter woruldlage<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.6-3"/> is botleas.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="64" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="352" ed="#liebermann"/>Husbryce. Husbryce ⁊ bærnet ⁊ open ðyfð ⁊ æbere morþ ⁊ hlafordswice æft<hi rend="italic">er</hi> woroldlage is botleas.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="64" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="352" ed="#liebermann"/>Husbrec ⁊ bærnet ⁊ open ðyfð ⁊ abere morð ⁊ hlafordswice æfter woruldlage is bótleas.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="64" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="353" ed="#liebermann"/>Husbrece<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.2"/> (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.3-2"/> est infractura domus) et bǽrnet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.4-2"/> (quod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.5-2"/> dicimus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.6-2"/> incendium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.3-2"/>) et ópen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.7"/> þyfþ<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.8"/> (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.3-2"/> est apertum furtum) et ǽbere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.9"/> morð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.10"/> (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.3-2"/> est apertum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.11"/> [probatum] murdrum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.12"/>) et hláfordspice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.13"/> (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.3-2"/> est infidelitas erga dominum) secundum legem seculi inemendabile est.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="64" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="353" ed="#liebermann"/>Destructio domus et combustio illius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.2-2"/> et publicus latro et mordrum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.3-4"/> et insidiator<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.4-4"/> proprii domini<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_64.lnote.oe.5-4"/> (traditor) transeunt omnem emendationem nec aliquam habent.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="64" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="353" ed="#liebermann"/>Domi fractura, combustura, manifestum furtum, patens mortificatura (scilicet clancula occisio que non possit negari) dominique prodicio secundum legem seculi carent emendatione.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="64" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="206" ed="#robertson"/>Husbryce. Husbryce ⁊ bærnet ⁊ open ðyfð ⁊ æbere morþ ⁊ hlafordswice æfter woroldlage is botleas.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="286" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Husbryce and bærnet and open þyfð and æbære morð and hlafordswyce æfter woruldlage is botleas.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="352" ed="#liebermann"/>(Hauseinbruch. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>). <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_64.lnote.de.1"/>Hauseinbruch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_64.lnote.de.2"/> und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_64.lnote.de.3"/> Brandstiftung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_64.lnote.de.4"/> und offenbar<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_64.lnote.de.5"/> erwiesener Diebstahl und unleugbarer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_64.lnote.de.6"/> heimlicher Mord und Verrath am Herrn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_64.lnote.de.7"/> ist nach staatlichem Recht unabbüssbar<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_64.lnote.de.8"/> [durch Geld].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Housebreaking. B) Housebreaking and arson and openly proven theft and undeniable secret murder and treachery against one's lord are, under secular law, not to be atoned for [with money].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_64.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="207" ed="#robertson"/>Assaults upon houses. According to secular law assaults upon houses<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_64.robnote.n.2"/>, arson<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_64.robnote.n.3"/>, theft which cannot be disproved, murder which cannot be denied and treachery towards a man's lord<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_64.robnote.n.4"/> are crimes for which no compensation can be paid<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_64.robnote.n.5"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="471" ed="#whitelock"/>House-breaking<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_64.whinote.n.4"/> and arson and obvious theft and manifest murder and betrayal of a lord are beyond compensation according to the secular law.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="287" ed="#rabin-doml"/>According to secular law, no compensation can be paid for housebreaking, arson, a theft which is openly proved, a murder which has been publicly discovered, or conspiracy against one’s lord.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 353, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Husbryce</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_64.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">353</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">parens <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">parens Hr</seg></note>
